WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.600
Cloud GPU workloads can become expensive quickly because they combine high-value accelerator capacity with fast-changing engineering demand.

2
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:14.000
A single experiment, notebook, training job, evaluation run, or inference deployment may be reasonable by itself.

3
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:20.000
The cost grows when many of those activities run without clear ownership, limits, or cleanup.

4
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.400
Idle time is one of the most common sources of waste.

5
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.800
A notebook can be open while no useful work is running.

6
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.200
A worker can wait for data while the GPU is allocated.

7
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.600
A training run can fail early but leave related resources behind.

8
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.600
The bill reflects allocated resources, not only productive model progress.

9
00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.800
GPU cost is also more than accelerator time.

10
00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:51.600
Datasets, checkpoints, logs, artifacts, managed orchestration, monitoring, storage snapshots, and data movement all affect the final cost.

11
00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:57.600
Production inference adds another pattern: cost follows demand, latency targets, scaling rules, and model efficiency.

12
00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:02.000
The practical lesson is that cost control is an engineering discipline.

13
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:08.800
It should be designed into workflow defaults, permissions, schedules, job queues, shutdown policies, monitoring, and review habits.

14
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:15.600
Waiting for a surprise bill before adding controls usually means the system is already hard to understand.

15
00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.000
Strong ownership matters.

16
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:25.600
Teams should know who owns a workload, why it exists, what value it supports, and when it should stop.

17
00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:32.000
When technical decisions are connected to financial impact, engineers can reduce waste without blocking useful work.

18
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:39.200
The best cost conversations are specific: which job, which owner, which purpose, which limit, and which cleanup rule.
